    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "In the Headlights: I Have No Idea"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p><b><font color='#ff0000'>Contains Mature Themes and Language</font></b></p>\n\n<p>I Have No Idea is a play with original music that explores\nadult ADHD through a story of neurodiversity, friendship,\nthe power of music, and how coffee makes everything\nbetter.</p>\n<p>Two actors portray four characters: Robin, a musician;\nBrian, a psychologist who doesn't believe in ADHD;\nTaylor, a barista and Robin's best friend; and Susan, the\npsychologist everyone needs in their corner.</p>\n<p>The play follows Robin and Taylor as they support each\nother through their ADHD journeys. Drawing on the lived\nexperiences of the playwright and creative team, it uses\nhumour, empathy, and music to explore the barriers\nneurodivergent people face, amplify ADHD voices,\nand offer insight into the lives of ADHDers. </p>\n\n<p><a href='https://intheheadlights.ca/' target='_blank'>intheheadlights.ca</a></p>\n\n"
      }
    ],
